<Viewbox xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
  xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
  Stretch="Uniform"
  StretchDirection="Both">
  <Grid Width="1560" Height="920" TextElement.Foreground="#D8DCE0" TextElement.FontFamily="Roboto">

    <Grid.RowDefinitions>
      <RowDefinition Height="76"/>
      <RowDefinition Height="1"/>
      <RowDefinition Height="*"/>
    </Grid.RowDefinitions>

    <TextBlock Grid.Row="0" Text="THE DECISION" FontSize="28" FontWeight="SemiBold" HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
    <Rectangle Grid.Row="1" Fill="#3E454B" Margin="22,0"/>

    <StackPanel Grid.Row="2" Orientation="Vertical" Margin="0,16,0,0">

      <Image Source="{Binding Assets[warwidens]}" Height="270" Stretch="Uniform" HorizontalAlignment="Center"/>

      <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" FontSize="17" LineHeight="27" Foreground="#D0D4D8" Margin="210,20,210,0" TextAlignment="Center">
        The Russian fleet is falling back to the west, toward the <Span FontWeight="SemiBold">Pillars of Hercules</Span>. The Mediterranean will be decided there.
        <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
        And the sonar logs from that night in the Tyrrhenian are still in your safe: the acoustic signature proving the torpedo that killed the <Span FontWeight="SemiBold">Oscar Austin</Span> was never European. You have the truth. You only have to decide what to do with it.
      </TextBlock>

      <Grid Margin="210,26,210,0">
        <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
          <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
          <ColumnDefinition Width="34"/>
          <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
        </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>

        <Border Grid.Column="0" Background="#141A1F" BorderBrush="#3E454B" BorderThickness="1" Padding="22,18">
          <StackPanel>
            <TextBlock Text="STAY SILENT" FontSize="20" FontWeight="SemiBold" Foreground="#C98A6A" HorizontalAlignment="Center" Margin="0,0,0,8"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" FontSize="15" LineHeight="23" Foreground="#B8BCC0" TextAlignment="Center">
              The Americans still believe the Russian lie and are blockading the Strait. You will have to break <Span FontWeight="SemiBold">two</Span> fleets at once.
            </TextBlock>
          </StackPanel>
        </Border>

        <Border Grid.Column="2" Background="#141A1F" BorderBrush="#3E454B" BorderThickness="1" Padding="22,18">
          <StackPanel>
            <TextBlock Text="SPEAK OUT" FontSize="20" FontWeight="SemiBold" Foreground="#8FBF7F" HorizontalAlignment="Center" Margin="0,0,0,8"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" FontSize="15" LineHeight="23" Foreground="#B8BCC0" TextAlignment="Center">
              The Sixth Fleet pulls back as a neutral observer. Only Russia ahead of you - but not a single shot at an American hull.
            </TextBlock>
          </StackPanel>
        </Border>
      </Grid>

      <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" FontSize="16" LineHeight="26" Foreground="#D0D4D8" Margin="200,24,200,0" TextAlignment="Center">
        Both options are waiting on the campaign map. <Span FontWeight="SemiBold" Foreground="#C98A6A">Open only the one you choose</Span>: the moment you commit to one, the other is gone for good and the war takes its course.
      </TextBlock>
    </StackPanel>
  </Grid>
</Viewbox>
